# Shell scripts and runit run scripts must be LF in the working tree on every
# platform. Windows runners default to core.autocrlf=true, and a CRLF checkout
# makes `bash -n` fail with "syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''"
# (GitHub Actions: core-host (Windows, full)) and would break a real Void
# install. `eol=lf` overrides core.autocrlf, so checkout stays LF everywhere.
*.sh text eol=lf
deployment/void/etc/sv/** text eol=lf
